Documentation for stack
-----------------------
rev 0.1, 6/4/99:  Initial release.  No behavioral verilog.


The stack generator is used to derive stack structures made up of
registers.  Multiple inputs are muxed in at the top of the stack.
Push and Pop operations cause the data to be moved, respectively,
further down or further up in the stack.  The output is driven from
the top-of-stack register.


GENERATOR ARGUMENTS:
--------------------
  NBITS:
    Definition:  
      The width of the data stored in the stack.  
    Legal Values:
      1 <= NBITS <= 128
    Default:
      32

  NInputs:
    Definition:
      The number of inputs to be muxed in at the first stage of the stack.
    Legal Values:
      1 <= NInputs <= 6
    Default:
      1

  Depth:
    Definition:
      The depth of the stack (number of registers it contains)
    Legal Values:
      1 <= Depth <= 128
    Default:
      8

  OutputSize:
    Definition:
      The drive strength of the final output driver.
    Legal Values:
      B, C, D, E
    Default:
      B
